                  '<h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>\n'
                  '<h3>Do I need to install an app to convert on my phone?</h3>\n'
                  '<p>No. The converter runs in your mobile browser, so Safari or Chrome is enough. You only need an '
                  'audio player if you want playlists or lock-screen controls.</p>\n'
                  '<h3>Why can I not find the MP3 in my iPhone Music app?</h3>\n'
                  '<p>iOS stores browser downloads in the Files app. The Music app only shows items added through your '
                  "computer's sync, so open the file from Files or import it into a file-based player.</p>\n"
                  '<h3>Which bitrate should I choose on a phone?</h3>\n'
                  '<p>128 kbps is fine for speech, and 192 kbps is a balanced choice for music on earbuds or a phone '
